ce","report":{"artifact_id":12239173519,"candidate":{"bundle_sha256":"9414b1a63333de90ea7d06ab0f656d1c1dd702e34ae25fca3b411831cbe331dd","changed":true,"changed_paths":["instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest.java"],"commit":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","commits":[{"changed_paths":["instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest.java"],"commit":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","parent":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","patch_sha256":"8a4b21853d0b323767fef61ac682e82330337c3dff04d6cc1fcf2f0e46b03ec0","subject":"Test InfluxDB chunk decoding failures without a failure consumer","tree":"d650ec5832d783d7cb862c6202a80c8a720ded93"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"8a4b21853d0b323767fef61ac682e82330337c3dff04d6cc1fcf2f0e46b03ec0","finding_commits":{"inline:4320869073":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","review:5580084717":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7"},"parent":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","patch_sha256":"8a4b21853d0b323767fef61ac682e82330337c3dff04d6cc1fcf2f0e46b03ec0","tree":"d650ec5832d783d7cb862c6202a80c8a720ded93"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"The overview's one open issue is addressed by an installed-agent chunked-query regression with an invalid results object and no failure consumer. The existing assertions require exactly one ERROR span and a duration histogram count of one, both with error.type=com.squareup.moshi.JsonDataException. All 10 lifecycle cases pass on baseline InfluxDB 2.14 and latest 2.25. Removing the decoder instrumentation makes the new test fail because the span incorrectly has UNSET status. The three issues listed as previously resolved require no additional changes.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5580084717"},{"analysis":"Added chunkedDecodingFailureWithoutFailureConsumer to InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest, using the normal query(QUERY, 1, consumer) overload and an HTTP-200 body whose results member is an object instead of an array. Reusing assertQuery verifies one ERROR client span and one duration observation with the decoding exception's error.type. The regression runs in the existing default/latest suite without new build wiring; dependencyInsight confirms the latest run uses influxdb-java 2.25. With the chunk processor instrumentation temporarily unregistered, this test fails with expected ERROR but actual UNSET; restored advice passes all 10 lifecycle cases. Formatting and Checkstyle pass.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4320869073"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"8c5949bec47e8c487998b7fc421e257cd2767f155f277842364594caeb5922ba","schema":2},"download_sha256":"a33b19f8ae3399668a2695301e3105355de5fd2e50eae73a16fcc4acf01440a4","frozen_sha":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","pr":20703,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"8c5949bec47e8c487998b7fc421e257cd2767f155f277842364594caeb5922ba","request_id":"4c3c27b6051b4b23aab28947045b94b5","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39363935916,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:a33b19f8ae3399668a2695301e3105355de5fd2e50eae73a16fcc4acf01440a4","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39366912584},"workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5566618546,5566651972,5566713561,5577451717,5578038543,5578376761,5580015794,5580024701,5580039812,5580084717],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nThe decoding-failure path without a failure consumer lacks an agent-backed regression.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add regression test for chunked-query decoding failure capture](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20703#discussion_r4320869073) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>3 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Preserve user exceptions thrown after cancellation](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20703#discussion_r4310130698)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Report intentional pre-response cancellation as success](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20703#discussion_r4310130680)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Register and label the exception-log test profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20703#discussion_r4310130658)\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5580084717","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5580084717},{"body":"[Testing] The new regressions do not exercise the decoding-failure path this advice adds: `FAILURE` is valid JSON containing a server-reported error, and user callback exceptions are captured separately by the wrappers. Losing this advice's failure capture could therefore go undetected. Add an agent-backed chunked-query regression in `InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest` with an invalid query-result shape and no failure consumer. Assert exactly one ERROR span and one duration observation, both with the decoding exception's `error.type`, and include it in the latest-dependency run to cover the newer-client behavior described here.","comment_commit_id":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","comment_id":4320869073,"key":"inline:4320869073","kind":"inline","line":39,"original_commit_id":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","original_line":39,"path":"instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbChunkProcessorInstrumentation.java","review_commit_id":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","review_id":5580084717,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-20T02:29:07Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"6ce5770d6dd286300c852babe193356aaf4fb2a15dd14a8f2985626119fd3ecf","id":4320869073,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-20T02:29:07Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86uLVXa"}],"frozen_at":1792466520,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-20T03:22:00Z","frozen_sha":"53e50041a419a1362b8011d52e64ad1e20c70bf1","head_ref":"copilot/split-20685-influxdb","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39363887052},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nSplits the InfluxDB changes from #20685, correcting query outcomes and duration timing without changing other integrations.\n\n- **Error classification:** Classify HTTP-200 top-level and per-statement errors with bounded `error.type`, never raw error text. Retain available HTTP error codes.\n- **Terminal completion:** End asynchronous and chunked operations exactly once after callbacks and chunk processing finish, retaining callback, transport, and decoding failures, including newer-client decoding failures without a failure consumer.\n- **Cancellation and compatibility:** Make the call available before failure consumers run so pre-response cancellation remains successful. Preserve `DONE` handling, callback parent context, and supported 2.4 APIs.\n- **Regression coverage:** Cover synchronous response errors, one asynchronous statement error, successful and failed chunked completion, cancellation before and after response delivery, callback failures after cancellation, and a single 2.4 statement-error case, with span and duration-metric assertions. Retain HTTP `400` assertions in the existing failing-query integration test.","title":"Fix InfluxDB query error classification and async completion"},"mode":"publish","pr":20703,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792466522,"generation":4,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"b80041c4df3c4d05a0856e28fcb1d087","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"4c3c27b6051b4b23aab28947045b94b5","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81","workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":39363935916,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/39363935916"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["ba399cd50d4866adb07072f29b61398f3d6e5dde968bc184347f0cd7dfcbe6f3"],"seen_inline_findings":["3e32339eb44fd53c4286b907aca8d9f003c39de16d6c00a69ffe24cae710b032"],"seen_missed_findings":[],"stage":"thread_effects","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39366912584}}